      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Below is a supplement.\n\nWith Undon sharp, the conditional compilation feature allows the user to define a variable that determines whether it is an Android build or not. For example, the sample code below\n\n#if <symbol defined with Android build>\n\nbool Quest = true;\n\n#else\n\nbool Quest = false;\n\n#endif\n\nI want Udon Graph, not Udon Sharp, and like Udon Sharp, I want a variable or API that can determine whether it is a Quest or not.\n\nFor example, the display problem of DinamicImage is caused by neglecting to convert the difference between the coordinate systems (right-handed system, left-handed system) between PC and Android. It's developed in C#, so I don't think it's that difficult to fix bugs, but it hasn't been fixed yet.\n\nWith this Api, it will be possible for users to take temporary measures against problems caused by lack of knowledge on the VRChat side of this kind of developer until official measures are released.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
